---
import BlogArticleShell from '../../../components/BlogArticleShell.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const canonicalPath = '/blog/kakobuy-t-shirts-spreadsheet-lane-guide-2026';
const publishedISO = '2026-06-10';
---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="T-shirts on the Kakobuy Spreadsheet: 2026 lane guide (streetwear, sizing, QC) | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="A data-backed tour of the t-shirt lane on kakobuy-cn.com—40 catalogue rows, 17 brand labels from BAPE to Gallery Dept., print QC checkpoints, and sizing discipline before paste."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="T-shirts lane guide: streetwear tees on the Kakobuy Spreadsheet (2026)"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="10 June 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'Kakobuy Spreadsheet t-shirts',
    'BAPE Gallery Dept tee guide 2026',
    'streetwear spreadsheet sizing',
    'print QC Kakobuy warehouse',
    'kakobuy-cn.com t-shirt lane',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    Tees are the volume lane of every haul—cheap enough to stack, risky enough that one wrong size ruins the carton economics.
    Our English <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> indexes <strong>40 t-shirt rows</strong> with <strong>17 brand labels</strong> in the deep pool behind <a href="/category/t-shirts/">T-Shirts</a> as of <strong>10 June 2026</strong>—here is how to browse them without treating a thumbnail as a size chart.
  </p>

  <h2>June 2026 t-shirt snapshot</h2>
  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Metric</th><th scope="col">T-shirts lane</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Indexed rows</td><td>40</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Distinct brand labels</td><td>17</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Most repeated</td><td>A Bathing Ape (6), Gallery Dept. (5), Amiri (4)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Also present</td><td>Chrome Hearts, Balenciaga, Burberry, Hellstar, Moncler</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Three tee clusters in our feed</h2>
  <h3>Graphic &amp; logo streetwear (BAPE, Hellstar, Chrome Hearts)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>A Bathing Ape</strong> leads row count—shark/camo motifs where print alignment is the QC battleground.
    <strong>Hellstar</strong> and <strong>Chrome Hearts</strong> trade on bold chest graphics; request flat-lay stills that show collar symmetry.
  </p>
  <h3>Distressed &amp; vintage aesthetics (Gallery Dept., Amiri)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Gallery Dept.</strong> and <strong>Amiri</strong> rows emphasise wash variance—warehouse photos should capture fade patterns you selected, not a random batch.
  </p>
  <h3>Luxury minimal (Balenciaga, Burberry, Moncler)</h3>
  <p>
    Lower graphic noise but tighter tolerance on neck label fonts and embroidery density.
  </p>

  <h2>Sizing before paste</h2>
  <p>
    Tees are the #1 return driver domestically.
    Pair every pick with <a href="/blog/kakobuy-sizing-spreadsheet-apparel/">spreadsheet sizing notes</a> and measure a shirt you already own—Asian size L is not US L.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Front/back print centre alignment and ink saturation</li>
    <li>Neck label stitch and tag font</li>
    <li>Shoulder seam drop vs size tag</li>
    <li>Hem length—oversized batches vary wildly</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Freight angle</h2>
  <p>
    Tees are freight-friendly fillers in mixed hauls—see <a href="/blog/group-haul-consolidation-freight-savings/">group haul consolidation</a>.
    Avoid using cheap tees to justify a cart full of heavy sneakers without re-quoting weight—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-sneakers-spreadsheet-lane-guide-2026/">sneakers lane guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet home</a></strong> → <a href="/category/t-shirts/">T-Shirts</a>.</li>
    <li>Freeze variant; paste via <a href="/blog/kakobuy-taobao/">Taobao</a> or <a href="/blog/kakobuy-weidian/">Weidian</a> hygiene.</li>
    <li>QC prints and labels; reject early while domestic return is cheap—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-domestic-returns-before-international-ship/">domestic returns</a>.</li>
    <li>Consolidate; ship using measured weight—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-to-parcel-checklist/">parcel checklist</a>.</li>
  </ol>
</BlogArticleShell>
